From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: foxnne <foxnne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:44:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] test: a fizzy suite for Wayland frame insets, on the protocol
 trace

The suite for "Wayland: frame insets, for a shadow the application draws round its own
decorations", `FizzyWayland` in test/testautomation_fizzy_wayland.c. Each test reconnects SDL to
the compositor with libwayland's request trace on (WAYLAND_DEBUG=client), stderr captured to a
file and libdecor off, makes a resizable borderless window with insets 24/6/30/40 round a 400x300
surface, presents into it with the GPU API so it maps, then parses the requests SDL sent on its
own objects (found by id with wl_proxy_get_id) at marks it wrote into the trace. The trace is read
between two marks where a window's objects are made again, as libwayland reuses the ids of
destroyed objects.

- floating: xdg_surface.set_window_geometry is the frame, the input region one rectangle, the
  frame and a band of min(inset, 8) round it, an opaque window's opaque region the frame, the
  published SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_FRAME_INSET_* are those asked for,
  xdg_toplevel.set_min_size/set_max_size are the frame's, and all of it follows
  SDL_SetWindowSize;
- maximized and fullscreen: the published insets are 0, the surface is the configured size, the
  window geometry and opaque region the whole surface and the input region nil; restored, the
  insets come back;
- a tooltip popup's positioner is anchored to the parent's frame, its offset less the parent's
  left and top insets, and SDL reports the popup where it was asked for;
- wayland_frameInsetsBeforeShow: a window made hidden publishes its insets before it is shown;
- wayland_frameInsetsRecreated: after an OpenGL ES renderer makes the shown window again through
  SDL_RecreateWindow, the new objects' window geometry, input region and opaque region are the
  frame's;
- wayland_frameInsetsShownAgain: hidden and shown again, the new xdg_surface gets the frame as its
  window geometry;
- wayland_frameInsetsInputMarginWide and ...None: the input band follows
  SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND_FRAME_INPUT_MARGIN_NUMBER (12, and 0).

On a release without the patch the properties are defined here, so the suite builds there and
fails on its first checks: nothing is published and no window geometry is sent. Headless weston
can't show a floating size the compositor chooses, toplevel bounds, tiled states, fractional scale
or xdg-decoration.
---
 test/testautomation_fizzy.h         |    1 +
 test/testautomation_fizzy_wayland.c | 1468 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 test/testfizzy.c                    |    1 +
 3 files changed, 1470 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 test/testautomation_fizzy_wayland.c

diff --git a/test/testautomation_fizzy.h b/test/testautomation_fizzy.h
index 6f9d7c6..7c31166 100644
--- a/test/testautomation_fizzy.h
+++ b/test/testautomation_fizzy.h
@@ -9,16 +9,17 @@
 #ifndef testautomation_fizzy_h_
 #define testautomation_fizzy_h_
 
 #include <SDL3/SDL_test.h>
 
 /* Test collections */
 extern SDLTest_TestSuiteReference fizzyGPUTestSuite;
 extern SDLTest_TestSuiteReference fizzyXkbTestSuite;
+extern SDLTest_TestSuiteReference fizzyWaylandTestSuite;
 
 /* Comma-separated GPU drivers ("metal,vulkan") a test must find: when one of
  * them is missing the test fails instead of being skipped. Set by testfizzy's
  * --require-gpu option, for CI runners that are known to have the driver.
